%% One deployment per account. [outside] = AWS console/CLI, IAM, or time.
%% Federation (on/off) and networking (fixed at create) are orthogonal attributes of Deployed/Ready.
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> Empty
    Empty --> Authorised: [outside] attach rendered deployer policy
    Authorised --> Deployed: admin deployment setup (any region, parent AMI resolved there)
    Authorised --> RolledBack: admin deployment setup, create fails
    RolledBack --> Empty: admin deployment teardown
    Deployed --> Ready: admin image build
    Deployed --> Deployed: admin deployment setup (update)
    Ready --> Ready: admin image build [--extension] (rebuild in place)<br/>admin deployment setup (update, image carried forward)
    Ready --> Ready: admin deployment setup --region B — refused, names the bucket's region<br/>image build from an older-base CLI — refused, upgrade the CLI
    Ready --> Dangling: [outside] AMI deregistered
    Dangling --> Ready: admin image build
    Ready --> Busy: baas run (job item launching…running)
    Busy --> Ready: instance records outcome + self-terminates<br/>Ctrl+C hook · poll cap · jobs terminate · watchdog
    Busy --> Busy: admin deployment teardown refused (names job ids)
    Deployed --> Empty: admin deployment teardown (bucket and table deleted with the stack)
    Ready --> Empty: admin deployment teardown — nothing survives<br/>(saves the extension, retires the image)
